# The off-server backup copy (infra/hetzner/README.md §7; offsite/offsite.sh). Copy to
# ${DOCS_CONFIG_DIR}/offsite.env, mode 0600, owned by root. Read by Compose for the `offsite` service.
# EVERY `<…>` IS A PLACEHOLDER; the job refuses to run while one remains.
#
# The bucket is at a DIFFERENT provider from the server (the readiness report proposes Backblaze B2,
# EU Central, with Scaleway as the alternative — both unverified until the console shows the region,
# versioning and Object Lock). Before filling this in, in the provider's console:
#   - a private bucket, versioning on (B2: always), Object Lock on if offered, in an EU region;
#   - a lifecycle rule keeping versions at least 35 days (the backup retention) plus a margin, and
#     aborting unfinished multipart uploads after 1 day;
#   - a key restricted to that bucket that can list, read and write but NOT delete
#     (B2: listBuckets, listFiles, readFiles, writeFiles — no deleteFiles, no bypassGovernance).
RCLONE_CONFIG_OFFSITE_TYPE=s3
# Backblaze B2 through its S3-compatible API (rclone provider "B2"); Scaleway: "Scaleway".
RCLONE_CONFIG_OFFSITE_PROVIDER=<required: B2 or Scaleway>
# https:// only. B2: https://s3.<region>.backblazeb2.com — the region is shown on the bucket page.
RCLONE_CONFIG_OFFSITE_ENDPOINT=<required: https://… the provider's S3 endpoint for the bucket's region>
RCLONE_CONFIG_OFFSITE_REGION=<required: the region, e.g. as shown in the provider's console>
RCLONE_CONFIG_OFFSITE_ACCESS_KEY_ID=<required: the restricted key's id>
RCLONE_CONFIG_OFFSITE_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=<required: the restricted key's secret>
OFFSITE_BUCKET=<required: the bucket name>
# One directory per environment, so TEST and production can never write into each other.
OFFSITE_PREFIX=munaxa-docs-test
# download (default): every new object is read back and its SHA-256 compared — the provider's own
# checksum is not trusted alone. Costs one download of each new file (provider egress).
OFFSITE_VERIFY=download
